                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                        "entry_id": "50e57e4a-dcc7-3d76-9e0f-733f430b3d0d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An instance of baying; a howl."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "200dbc3a-9291-4384-a0de-1bf34e20cb5e",
                                "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                                "text": "1877, Charles Cayley (translator), Homer Iliad, book XXI\nSoon as he hears bayings, and is not alarm'd nor affrighted..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47ae27e5-0f91-4bb4-9897-c25e740f306a",
                                "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                                "text": "...the distressed bayings of his dogs, ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4dc3ccd7-b730-401d-9a36-1dbced8ef5ae",
                                "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                                "text": "And the thrill which their ill-omened bayings send through people at large is a measure of the state of tension in which the general mind is held."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13cdf2b7-113b-4d81-9fdb-080e4fe38a45",
                                "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                                "text": "When I had advanced some distance into the forest, I heard the notes of the bugle and the distant baying of hounds in full cry, which gradually ceased, till nothing but a faint echo of the bugle reached my ear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c9a2004-0d88-4b6a-ad8c-004cf7cb147f",
                                "sense_id": "9e15403d-90cb-3e95-9db5-aa61831480e8",
                                "text": "1907, Frank Justus Miller (translator), Seneca, Hercules Furens Act III\nWho, tossing back and forth his triple heads,/ With mighty bayings watches o'er the realm."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
